1. System Identity

Name: Astrometric Simulation Engine (ASE)Domain: Proton–Laser Interaction, Cosmic Data Integration, Multi‑Scale Plasma SimulationPurpose: Provide a unified computational instrument linking astrophysical environmental datasets with microphysical proton‑laser physics.

2. High‑Level Summary

ASE is a research‑grade simulation framework integrating:

Cosmic Data Pipelines

Plasma‑Laser Solvers

HPC Acceleration Layers

Zero‑Trust Security Architecture

Scientific Visualization & Workflow Tools

The system enables proton‑laser simulations under astrophysical boundary conditions, supporting research in cosmic‑ray acceleration, plasma astrophysics, and high‑energy particle transport.

